1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,926
Thank you for finishing this.

2
00:00:01,926 --> 00:00:06,328
Most people who start a course like this don't, and you built four working agents

3
00:00:06,328 --> 00:00:09,481
and a fifth one of your own instead of just watching mine.

4
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:11,875
Look back at where this started.

5
00:00:11,875 --> 00:00:16,660
An inbox with forty unread emails and a renewal that was six days from being missed

6
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,179
entirely.

7
00:00:17,179 --> 00:00:21,964
You now have a working method for turning a task like that into something a machine

8
00:00:21,964 --> 00:00:25,135
can carry, and the judgement to know when it shouldn't.

9
00:00:25,685 --> 00:00:30,472
If one of these five has to carry the rest, make it the third: trial before trust,

10
00:00:30,472 --> 00:00:31,990
every time, no exceptions.

11
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,675
Everything else in this course is a technique.

12
00:00:34,675 --> 00:00:38,762
That one is the discipline that keeps the techniques from hurting you.

13
00:00:39,312 --> 00:00:44,614
If this saved you real hours, a review is what puts this course in front of the next

14
00:00:44,614 --> 00:00:46,823
person stuck where you were at 0.1.

15
00:00:46,823 --> 00:00:51,305
And if you're stuck on your own build, the Q&A tab reaches me directly.

16
00:00:51,305 --> 00:00:53,072
Go automate the second task.
